I am very happy to inform you that today  we reach an agreement on the automatic  exchange of information in the field of  Taxation in relation to reportable  cross-border arrangements we are happy  to see an agreement on this point  because the measures foreseen in this  proposal will help Member States protect  their tax bases from erosion erosion and  consequently protect the revenues to the  national budgets today we also updated  the euro list of non cooperative  jurisdictions for tax purposes the  conceived agreed to add three countries  the Bahamas st. Kitts and Nevis and the  US Virgin Island we also agreed to add  another four countries Anguilla Antilla  and Barbuda in the British Virgin  Islands and Dominic Dominica together  with my colleagues we agreed on the euro  position for g20 finance ministers and  central bank governors meeting which  will take place in a week in Buenos  Aires in my role of a president of the  echo fin calcio I will have the honor to  represent the you together with  colleagues from the European Commission  and the European Central Bank I would  like to say a few words on the risk  reduction banking package the presidency  has worked very hard with the  delegations to find a compromise  satisfactory to all Member States but  some more time is needed today the  European Union has reiterated its  commitment to bring more transparency to  the world of aggressive tax planning we  are global frontrunners in this field  and European Union of course will use  its political influence to push for a  similar action in the international  level
 

